        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Divide first for $7(a+8)=28$, since 7 is a factor of 28. Expand first for $7(a+8)=30$, since dividing by 7 first introduces a fraction.",
          "worked": "For $7(a+8)=28$, divide both sides by 7 first to get $a+8=4$ without expanding. For $7(a+8)=30$, expand first to get $7a+56=30$ and avoid an intermediate fraction.",
